# Supabase (Exhibition)

**Full reference:** [docs/supabase-infrastructure.md](docs/supabase-infrastructure.md)

## Live stack (do not use supabase-local)

- Host: `192.168.0.146` — project **`cashbook`**, dir `~/apps/cashbook` on server
- API: `:54321` · Postgres: `:54322` · Studio: `:54323` (`supabase_*_cashbook` containers)
- **Wrong path:** `~/supabase-local/supabase` (separate volume; not the running stack)

## Exhibition

- Schema: `exhibition` (Supabase clients use `db.schema: "exhibition"`)
- `.env`: `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=http://192.168.0.146:54321`
- Verify: `npm run db:check`

## Never

- `supabase db reset` or `docker volume rm` on `supabase_db_cashbook`
- Re-run `20260421_exhibition_schema.sql` if schema exists (drops all exhibition tables)

## Repairs (host only, data-safe)

```bash
cd ~/apps/cashbook
# crash-loop: docker stop supabase_db_cashbook && sudo rm -f .../postmaster.pid
docker ps -aq --filter name=cashbook | xargs -r docker rm -f  # if start conflicts
supabase stop && supabase start
```

`PGRST002` = Postgres down, not an app bug. Script: `scripts/repair-shared-supabase.sh` (sync repo to server first).
